SENTINEL memory specs
---------------------

The SENTINEL is equipped with 128 KiB of RAM and 4 KiB of ROM.
The 64 KiB address space of the Z80 is mapped as low RAM (0000-7FFF, A15 low)
and high RAM (8000-FFFF, A15 high).

The 128 KiB RAM are divided into 4 banks of 32 KiB each:
- bank 0: 00000-07FFF
- bank 1: 08000-0FFFF
- bank 2: 10000-17FFF
- bank 3: 18000-1FFFF

Bank 0 is always fixed as low RAM.
Banks 1, 2 and 3 can be selected as high RAM and ROM can be switched out
(see configuration register specs).
Memory banks 2 and 3 are not used in R1.

Please note that only SRAM chips that provide both a /CS1 and a CS2 pin can be
used. Chips without a CS2 pin cannot be used with this setup.

All addresses are given in hexadecimal notation.

Bill of materials:
- 128 KiB SRAM
- 4 KiB UVEPROM or EEPROM (2732 or compatible)
- 74HC08 quad 2-input AND gates
- 74HC32 quad 2-input OR gates
- 2x DIP-14 socket (optional)
- 1x DIP-24 socket (optional)
- 1x DIP-32 socket (optional)
- 3x capacitor 100 nF

